  "customfield_10187": null,
  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Currently only an ingest cleans up after itself if it fails, by removing artefacts created during the ingest (objectStore, datastreamStore, registry, fieldSearch, resourceIndex).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If an operation fails part-way through, then anything added during the operation should be removed, to prevent inconsistencies eg between the registry, objectStore and datastreamStore.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "NB the objective of this is NOT to introduce full transactioning including rollback, it is to ensure consistency.  Particularly the canonical store (objectStore, datastreamStore) should be left in a consistent state.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
