  "customfield_10187": null,
  "description": "<p>Currently only an ingest cleans up after itself if it fails, by removing artefacts created during the ingest (objectStore, datastreamStore, registry, fieldSearch, resourceIndex).</p>\n\n<p>If an operation fails part-way through, then anything added during the operation should be removed, to prevent inconsistencies eg between the registry, objectStore and datastreamStore.</p>\n\n<p>NB the objective of this is NOT to introduce full transactioning including rollback, it is to ensure consistency.  Particularly the canonical store (objectStore, datastreamStore) should be left in a consistent state.</p>",
